    "notes": "ASSUMPTIONS FOR THIS EXAMPLE (Raspberry Pi 4 Model B, full CPU load, board in a closed case)\nValues are illustrative, chosen to be plausible and to exercise every flag. Replace with datasheet or measured values for real work.\nL x W for U1, U2, U4, U5, U6 and J1 are the body sizes in 'Raspberry Pi 4 Model B.STEP'. U3 uses the STEP body (5.4 mm). L1, L2 are not in the STEP.\nU1: VDD_CORE about 0.88 V at 3.6 A under full load. θja 14 °C/W is a bare-board, still-air estimate; T max 85 °C is the throttle point.\nU3 (PMIC) has one row per output rail, as the Q methods tab asks. Each row's density, share and margin are for that rail only; the package total is the sum of the four rows (about 1.04 W).\nU3 buck efficiencies are read at the stated load, not the headline peak. Buck input is the 5V0 rail (5.1 V).\nU6: average current at a mixed Wi-Fi duty cycle. New class 'RF / wireless module' added on the Q methods tab (row 34).\nL1, L2: I squared R on DCR only; core loss not included. No θja, so their margin is not checked, only density.\nJ1: R is the VBUS plus GND contact loop resistance (0.03 Ω). Measured board input power on the Rail budget tab is 5.1 V x 1.35 A = 6.9 W."
